  PURPOSE
  =================
  Spec-aligned reference XML. Every element labelled with its Significance,
  Cardinality, and Data Type / max length per the v0.2 spec.

  ANNOTATION FORMAT
  =================
  Each element comment carries three pieces:
    [M | O | C]                       Significance:
                                        M = Mandatory
                                        O = Optional
                                        C = Conditional Mandatory
                                            (mandatory only when its condition holds)
    Cardinality                       e.g. "1", "0..1", "0..*", "1..2"
    Data type / length                e.g. "String(50)", "DateTime", "Grouping"

  SIGNIFICANCE PRECEDENCE RULE (from spec README)
  =================
  "Significance takes precedence over Cardinality where they conflict.
   If a Mandatory child field sits within an Optional parent, the child is
   only Mandatory when the parent is mapped."

  CARDINALITY KEY
  =================
    1        Exactly one occurrence
    0..1     Zero or one
    0..*     Zero or many (e.g. multiple addresses, phones, NOKs)
    1..2     Exactly one or two (only used by patient.identification)

  RULE — NO EMPTY TAGS
  =================
  Per Synapxe Guide v0.42 (page 10) and putEvent README:
    Source must EXCLUDE all empty XML tags for unmapped fields and mapped
    fields with no values populated. Do not emit <tag></tag>, <tag/>, or
    <tag>NA</tag>. Omit the element entirely.
================================================================================
-->
